# "If it's a creature card of the chosen type, you may reveal it and put it into your hand" - the "may" answered No:
# the Goblin Piker on top of Bot1's library stays there, unrevealed, and is drawn in the draw step (the 2017-08-25
# ruling). The matching Goblin Pikers in Bot2's hand and on top of Bot2's library are not Bot2's to reveal here: they
# stay in Bot2's zones, and Bot2's hand is not touched.

